#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0176 expect=skipped domain=ADLBC
#note "ABLFL is not declared at all. The rule has no Requirements.Variables gate, so it still EXECUTES; the absent column reads as all-missing and the leading `not empty(ABLFL)` is false on every row - the negation is what stops the bare-empty broadcast fold from producing a dataset-level violation. This pins that ABLFL's outright absence is PMDA-AD0127A's business, not this rule's. PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms phase 4: the rule now declares the gate variable in Requirements.Variables.All, so the absent column takes the auditable SKIP this scenario pins (Fix #330 remedy: a presence rule reports the absence once)."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 2.5
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALT | 7.0
